Displays an '''INACTIVE''' status badge and, in the main namespace, files the page under the matching activity category. Used on utaite and group pages. See {{T|Active}} for the opposite state.

==Syntax==
{{T|Inactive|block=1
|v1=nocat =
|v2=groups =
}}

==Examples==
* {{T|Inactive|_Y_=1|p1=nocat = true}}
* <code><nowiki>This utaite is {{Inactive}}.</nowiki></code> — badge '''and''' categorizes as an inactive singer
* <code><nowiki>{{Inactive|groups=true}}</nowiki></code> — badge and categorizes as an inactive '''group'''

{| class="dataTable sortable"
! Parameter !! Aliases !! Label !! Description !! Type !! Default !! Status
|-
| <code>nocat</code> || – || No category || Set to <code>true</code> to show the badge '''without''' categorizing (use in docs and examples). || string || – ||
|-
| <code>groups</code> || – || Group || Set to <code>true</code> to categorize into [[:Category:Inactive Groups]] instead of [[:Category:Inactive Singers]]. || string || – ||
|}

